A||||7||mrfixit58||Slam When put into DRIVE! Help!||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||02-01-2001||01:58 PM||||I'm looking at buying an SE. It's a V6 automatic. It runs good, drives straight and smooth and stops straight. The only problem besides a bad case of UG-LY is it seems to slam into gear when going from park to reverse and from neutral to drive. Is this the TCC solenoid or some other gizmo?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-01-2001||02:11 PM||||could be just idleing too fast. Let it warm up and see if it still does it. I dont know a whole lot about Fiero autos (god, i wish mine was)||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierojunky||02-01-2001||02:14 PM||||is it being parked on a hill??  If so be sure the emergency brake is being used.  It its just being put in park the car will drift alittle putting strain on the transmission - thus causing the thunk when you take it out of park||||reg||6
Z||000003||Oreif||02-01-2001||02:15 PM||||If the TCC was bad and locked the car would die once you put it in gear. Sounds like the idle is too high.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-01-2001||02:56 PM||||check all the motor/tranny mounts. One or more has probalby torn.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||02-01-2001||03:07 PM||||According to the tach, it was idling about 1200 rpm. How would I lower the idle? The car was on level ground (I'm in Florida!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) so thats not it. The car seems to shift alright while your driving it. <P>I wish it was a close ratio 4-speed. This is the one we're think of making into a off-roader. Can't complain, the asking price is only $500 but I think I can get it for $350 -$400. The car doesn't even have any exhaust leaks, the a/c has been converted to 134a and WORKS!<P>If I buy it, I'll definatly check out the transmission mounts.<P>Thanks guys,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||02-01-2001||05:30 PM||||also check the dogbone. mine looked fine but only a tiny bit of looseness makes it really thunk. It was so bad I thought axle was bad<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||02-01-2001||10:32 PM||||my bet would be motor mounts + dog bone bushings.  One failing will cause the others to go bad in a hurry.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
